Process and verification record
Document due diligence
The five Jeeves attachments were read. “Jeevie R1JP” and “Jeevie Review Instrument” both contain RI-JP document-review text; the actual RI-JV1 behavioral battery was not supplied. PRECHECK’s Jeeves report describes a staged reconstruction. The Master remained at engine selection. Structured output and adoption of a document therefore did not establish factual correctness or a passed behavioral baseline.
PRECHECK Master, its two supplied family packs and Appendix 4 were reviewed. The family packs govern Synthesis outputs or PRECHECK’s own artifacts, not this research proposal. A one-off rule set was used rather than imposing every family requirement. The fiction-review instrument was not claimed to have been executed verbatim on the research packet.
Mechanical checks and limits
The first packet passed 20 encoded mechanical checks. The revised v0.2 passed 25 after rule updates for its version, six references, comparator, blinding and history removal. The one-off Python checks covered structure, versions, references, arithmetic and selected required/forbidden strings. They did not validate factual truth, novelty, semantics, scoring quality, model behavior or scientific readiness. Six final v0.2 pages were visually checked; the audit archive preserves the original run and later reruns.
External review handling
An identical v0.2 packet was intended for fresh reviewer sessions, without exposing prior returns. Five returns were pasted without model names. They are R1–R5 in order; 37 numbered findings were recorded, with original severity and an assessment. No independent-family convergence count is justified until model metadata is supplied.
R1 disclosed automatic contextual summaries and no history retrieval. R2 did not browse. R3 claimed primary browsing but did not provide an explicit prior-exposure disclosure in the pasted text. R4 declared a cold read and incomplete exact S4 extraction. R5 disclosed opening two saved notes before reading, departing from the no-history-retrieval request. These are recorded as supplied self-reports; findings were assessed individually.
What was done with the returns
The assistant reconstructed the common question, grouped overlapping issues, retained singleton objections, checked findings against v0.2, verified consequential research claims against primary sources where accessible, and separated the comparison from its own recommendation. It did not adopt reviewer repairs by vote, rerun the experiment, or change v0.2. The complete 37-entry assessment register is appended to this checkpoint.

